1- Deploy Caldera Server

Prepare a Linux VM (Ubuntu 24.04 recommended).

Clone the Caldera repository:

git clone https://github.com/mitre/caldera.git --recursive
cd caldera

Create a Python virtual environment:

python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate

Install dependencies:

pip install -r requirements.txt

Start the Caldera server:

python server.py

Access the web interface at:

http://:(PortNumber)

Default login: admin / admin

Change the password immediately for security.

2- Add a Windows Agent (Red Team Agent)

Navigate to Agents → Add Agent in Caldera.

Fill in the details:

Agent name: Win10-RedTeam

Platform: Windows

Group: Optional

Server IP: Caldera server IP

Generate the agent installer script.

On the Windows VM turn off windows defender and then run the script in PowerShell as Administrator.

The agent should connect automatically to Caldera and appear in the agent list.

3- Verify Connection

Check the agent is listed in Caldera → Agents → Active.

Confirm the agent is reporting its status and can receive tasks.

4- Notes

Ensure Windows firewall allows outbound connections to the Caldera server.

Agents will be used to execute controlled attacks to test Wazuh detection.
